From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sprd: put drivers/staging/sprd/sfp on its own include path

Second build stop of the same kind, this time in the vendor SFP
(Stateless Flow Processing / IPA offload) driver:

  drivers/staging/sprd/sfp/sfp_tuple.c:35:10: error: 'sfp.h' file not
      found with <angled> include; use "quotes" instead
  #include <sfp.h>

Every other file in that directory includes the header as "sfp.h"; only
sfp_tuple.c uses angle brackets, and the Makefile never puts its own
directory on the include path, so the angled form cannot resolve.

This is not dead code: the shipping kernel of this very firmware contains
102 sfp_* symbols in artifacts/System.map, i.e. the vendor build did
compile this driver.  The published Makefile is simply missing the flag
(no public branch has it either), so add the standard

  ccflags-y += -I$(src)

Build-only change: it adds an include directory and does not alter the
objects produced.

 drivers/staging/sprd/sfp/Makefile | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/sprd/sfp/Makefile b/drivers/staging/sprd/sfp/Makefile
index e24c63d848e9..7648f674a222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/sprd/sfp/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/staging/sprd/sfp/Makefile
@@ -11,3 +11,9 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_SPRD_SFP_SUPPORT)  += sfp_ipa.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SPRD_IPA_V3_SUPPORT)  += sfp_netlink.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SPRD_IPA_V3_SUPPORT)  += sfp_filter.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SPRD_SFP_TEST)  += sfp_test.o
+
+# sfp_tuple.c includes <sfp.h>, and sfp.h itself includes "sfp_hash.h";
+# the shipping kernel builds this driver (102 sfp_* symbols in System.map),
+# so the published Makefile is simply missing its own directory on the
+# include path.
+ccflags-y += -I$(src)
-- 
